solution.text:
The half life $\mathrm{t}_{1 / 2}=10$ days The decay constant
$$
\mathrm{k}=\frac{0.693}{\mathrm{t}_{1 / 2}}=\frac{0.693}{10 \text { days }}=0.0693 \text { days }^{-1}
$$
The time required for one fourth conversion
$$
\begin{aligned}
&\mathrm{t}=\frac{2.303}{\mathrm{k}} \log _{10} \frac{\mathrm{a}}{\mathrm{a}-\mathrm{x}} \\
&=\frac{2.303}{0.0693 \text { day }^{-1}} \log _{10} \frac{1}{1-(1 / 4)}=4.1 \text { days }
\end{aligned}
$$
